# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except .env.production, which is committed on purpose. It holds only NEXT_PUBLIC_* build-time
# flags — values that Next inlines into the client bundle at `next build`, so they are shipped to
# every browser regardless and are not secrets by construction. It is committed rather than set as
# a Pterodactyl egg variable because the build happens inside the *install* container, which does
# not reliably receive the server's configured env vars (this is what caused the DATABASE_URL
# trouble documented in PLANNING.md) — a variable set in the panel can therefore silently fail to
# reach the build, with no error and no working feature. A file in git always reaches it.
# Real secrets (AUTH_SECRET, RESEND_API_KEY, GOOGLE_*, CHAT_BROADCAST_SECRET) stay out of git and
# stay in the panel: they are read at runtime, where the panel's variables do arrive correctly.
!.env.production

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

/app/generated/prisma

# rotating DB snapshots written by scripts/backupDb.ts — machine-local data, not source
/backups

# user-uploaded Doc images — machine-local content, not source (see app/api/uploads/image)
/public/uploads

# DATABASES. This is not a tidiness entry — it is load-bearing.
#
# The Pterodactyl install script ends with `git clean -fd`, which deletes untracked files. Ignored
# files are spared (removing those needs -x), so these entries are the only thing standing between
# the live database and every Re-install. Without them, each Re-install silently wiped all
# production data — which is what kept leaving sessions orphaned ("Not authenticated" on every
# action while apparently logged in) and forced workspaces to be recreated over and over.
#
# NOTE THE PATH. Production's DATABASE_URL is `file:./siqt.db`, which reads like the repo root but
# is NOT: Prisma resolves a relative SQLite path against the SCHEMA FILE's directory, so the real
# database lives at `prisma/siqt.db`. A first attempt at this fix ignored `/siqt.db` and protected
# nothing at all — caught only by looking for the file on the server and finding it one directory
# down. Match on the whole directory rather than one filename so a renamed or newly-added database
# can't silently fall outside this again.
#
# Never run `git clean -fdx` against a production checkout: `-x` removes ignored files too, which
# defeats all of this.
/prisma/*.db
/prisma/*.db-journal
/prisma/*.db-wal
/prisma/*.db-shm
